.\" man/man3/Docv::Colors.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Colors" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Colors \- Named roff colors: the eight ANSI colors and \fB\%default\fR, plus the colors a page defines with \fB\%.defcolor\fR as 24\-bit values (the screen maps them to fewer colors when the terminal shows fewer).
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBmodule Docv::Colors\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Named roff colors: the eight ANSI colors and \fB\%default\fR, plus the colors
a page defines with \fB\%.defcolor\fR as 24\-bit values (the screen maps them to
fewer colors when the terminal shows fewer).
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBNAMES\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
NAMES = {
  "default" => Color::DEFAULT,
  "black" => Color.palette(0),
  "red" => Color.palette(1),
  "green" => Color.palette(2),
  "yellow" => Color.palette(3),
  "blue" => Color.palette(4),
  "magenta" => Color.palette(5),
  "cyan" => Color.palette(6),
  "white" => Color.palette(7),
}
.EE
.RE
.RE
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.[]?(name : String) : Color | Nil\fR
Looks up a color by roff name; unknown names yield \fB\%nil\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.define(name : String, scheme : String, value : String) : Nil\fR
Defines \fIname\fR from a roff color specification (\fB\%rgb \%#rrggbb\fR,
\fB\%gray\fR/\fB\%grey\fR and \fB\%cmyk\fR schemes).
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/style.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "Docv" (3cr),
.BR "docv" (7cr)
